# Line endings.
#
# This repository is edited on Windows and deployed to Linux. The committed
# blobs are all correctly LF today — these rules pin that, so a workstation with
# a different core.autocrlf setting cannot quietly change it.
#
# What that guards against: a shell script committed with CRLF, which bash on
# Ubuntu rejects on its very first line with
#
#     $'\r': command not found
#
# — for a root-run bootstrap script, on a fresh server, in an error that names
# nothing useful. Anything the server executes or parses is pinned to LF.

* text=auto

# Executed or parsed on the server — must be LF.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
.env*       text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.db        binary
*.sqlite    binary
*.xlsx      binary
*.pdf       binary
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.ico       binary
